@page "/khamsin/install"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Install Khamsin - WaxUI</PageTitle>

<div class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Install Khamsin</h1>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">Add the Khamsin build-time utility CSS engine to a Blazor project.</p>
</div>

<div class="space-y-8">

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-muted border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Package</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            Khamsin 0.3.3 bundles library CSS into <code class="bg-card px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">khamsin.css</code>
            and emits a Tailwind-compatible preflight. The package carries the runtime, the analyzer and
            manifest generator, the MSBuild task and its
            <code class="bg-card px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">buildTransitive</code> props and targets.
            WaxUI targets this version.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mt-3">
            <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-[3px]"
               href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Khamsin">nuget.org/packages/Khamsin</a>
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Add the package</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            Install Khamsin into every project that writes Khamsin classes.
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>dotnet add package Khamsin --version 0.3.0</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4 mb-2">Or add the reference by hand:</p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>&lt;ItemGroup&gt;
  &lt;PackageReference Include="Khamsin" Version="0.3.0" /&gt;
&lt;/ItemGroup&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Add the imports</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            Make <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">KhamsinClass</code> and the
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">Kx</code> helpers available to components.
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>@@using Khamsin</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Load the stylesheet</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            The build task generates <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">khamsin.css</code> and
            registers it as a static web asset. The file contains the theme, preflight, library CSS and
            the utilities this app renders. Link it like any other stylesheet:
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>@@* App.razor *@@
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="khamsin.css" /&gt;</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4 mb-2">
            A Blazor Server app can serve the generated file from an endpoint instead, with a content
            hash and a one-year immutable cache policy:
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>app.MapKhamsinCss();</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4">
            On .NET 11 the static-web-assets compression pass rejects Khamsin's registration. Set
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">KhamsinRegisterStaticWebAsset</code> to
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">false</code> and use the endpoint. The
            WaxUI docs app does exactly that.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Theme tokens</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            A library can ship its own <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">khamsin.json</code>.
            Khamsin embeds that config in the assembly, and every consuming app merges it under its own
            configuration, so semantic classes such as
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">bg-primary</code>,
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">text-foreground</code> and
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">font-display</code> validate and emit without
            being copied into the app.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-2">Values can stay in CSS custom properties:</p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{
  "dark": ".theme-dark",
  "colors": { "primary": "var(--primary)" }
}</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4">
            Merge order is built-in defaults, then referenced libraries in assembly-name order, then the
            app's own <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">khamsin.json</code>. The app always
            wins, so overriding one library token does not require restating the rest.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
            A library can also list stylesheets under
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">css</code> in its configuration. Those files
            are embedded with the config and emitted in the base layer, so consumers still link only
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">khamsin.css</code>.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Give a component defaults</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            Components expose a <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">Khamsin</code> parameter by
            inheriting from <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">KhamsinComponentBase</code> and
            concatenating their defaults with it.
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>@@inherits KhamsinComponentBase

&lt;button type="button" class="@@(Defaults + Khamsin)"&gt;@@ChildContent&lt;/button&gt;

@@code {
    private static readonly KhamsinClass Defaults = "rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_-_2px)] bg-ocean-600 px-4 py-2 text-white";

    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4 mb-2">Consumers then override only what they need:</p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>&lt;PrimaryButton Khamsin=&quot;@@("px-6")&quot;&gt;Save&lt;/PrimaryButton&gt;</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">px-6</code> wins over the default
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">px-4</code> at runtime. Both classes are in the
            stylesheet because both are literals in the source.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Verify the install</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            Build a web or executable project. The task writes the stylesheet after compilation:
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-muted rounded-[calc(var(--radius)_+_4px)] p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>dotnet build
# obj/&lt;configuration&gt;/&lt;tfm&gt;/khamsin.css</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
            Open the file and check that it contains the classes your markup actually uses, for
            example <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">.px-6</code> and
            <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">.p-4</code>. Referenced libraries do not emit CSS by
            default; they carry manifests, and the consuming app collects the classes of the
            components it renders.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Build settings</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            All settings are optional. Set them in the project file or on the command line.
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead>
                    <tr class="border-b border-border">
                        <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left text-muted-foreground font-medium">Property</th>
                        <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left text-muted-foreground font-medium">Default</th>
                        <th class="py-2 text-left text-muted-foreground font-medium">Purpose</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr class="border-b border-border">
                        <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-foreground font-medium"><code>KhamsinEmitCss</code></td>
                        <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted-foreground">true for web/executable projects</td>
                        <td class="py-3 text-muted-foreground">Emit the stylesheet for this project.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="border-b border-border">
                        <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-foreground font-medium"><code>KhamsinCssFileName</code></td>
                        <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted-foreground">khamsin.css</td>
                        <td class="py-3 text-muted-foreground">File name registered as a static web asset.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-foreground font-medium"><code>KhamsinRegisterStaticWebAsset</code></td>
                        <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted-foreground">true</td>
                        <td class="py-3 text-muted-foreground">Register the generated file with the static web asset pipeline.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-card border border-border">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">Troubleshooting</h2>
        <ul class="list-none space-y-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <li>
                <span class="text-foreground font-medium">NU1101: package not found.</span>
                The package id or version does not match nuget.org, or the feed is unavailable.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="text-foreground font-medium">KHM001.</span>
                A class expression is not a literal. Use <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">Kx.When</code>
                or <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">Kx.Variant</code>, or move runtime values into
                CSS custom properties such as <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">w-(--w)</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="text-foreground font-medium">KHM002.</span>
                The class is not in the utility registry. Check the supported utilities reference.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="text-foreground font-medium">A library component has no styles.</span>
                The consuming app must reference Khamsin and must actually render the component;
                unused components contribute nothing.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="text-foreground font-medium">khamsin.css returns 404.</span>
                Confirm the project emits CSS (<code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">KhamsinEmitCss</code>)
                and that the link matches <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">KhamsinCssFileName</code>,
                or map the endpoint with <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded-[0.25rem]">MapKhamsinCss()</code>.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div>
